        "original_id": "372b7bc8-2ce3-5e92-a7b3-88372b651bc6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006\n- People: Jennifer Granholm, Dick DeVos, Ruth Johnson\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan, lieutenant governor candidate, running mate\n- Places: Michigan\n\nFacts:\n- The Michigan gubernatorial election of 2006 was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held on November 7, 2006.\n- Jennifer Granholm was the incumbent Democratic Governor of Michigan in the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election.\n- Jennifer Granholm was re-elected in the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- Ruth Johnson was the 2006 Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.\n- Ruth Johnson was a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives.\n- Dick DeVos, born on October 21, 1955, is an American entrepreneur-businessman and author from Michigan.",
